From 8fd66ab5b0053fa0da5322a82d8794a468510878 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 08:29:08 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] fix(turning): read the holder side without a thread's
 antipodal arc ends

The thread kernel winds each pass in half-turn XY arcs about the axis
whose ends alternate onto the antipode, so the raw from/to reading put
every threading path on both sides of the spindle and refused it (and
its drawn body). The holder side is now read from the moves' meridian
pieces with round arcs about the axis left out (a meridian arc's chords
count, catching a bulge past its ends), and those round arcs are read
at |rho| on the holder's side. A near side off the axis while the far
side reaches under twice PAST_CENTRE is refused instead of guessed.

Pinned by a_thread_pass_winding_through_the_antipode_is_judged_not_refused,
the_drawn_body_flips_its_radial_with_the_holder_side and the extended
the_side_is_where_the_path_reaches_and_a_past_centre_overrun_keeps_it.

Refs #1102

